:cia-world-factbook"}, "contributor": "encyclopedia:cia-world-factbook", "license": "public-domain", "license_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/about/copyright-and-contributors/", "source_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/countries/mi/", "revision": "factbook.json", "historical": false}, {"id": "enc-cia-mi-6", "text": "Members of the Yao ethnic group -- which had long traded with Malawi from Mozambique -- introduced Islam and began to settle in Malawi in significant numbers in the mid-1800s, followed by members of the Lomwe ethnic group.", "tier": "anchor", "state": "anchor", "trust": "trusted", "sfe": {"Phi": 1, "eps": 0.0, "mu": 1.0}, "packet": {"schema": "FORGE-RESONANCE-PACKET/v1", "Phi": 1, "eps": 0.0, "mu": 1.0, "sfe": {"Phi": 1, "eps": 0.0, "mu": 1.0}, "placed_by": "athena", "standing": "anchor", "phi_basis": "ingestion placement; factual anchor, phase Φ1"}, "concepts": ["A.MALAWI"], "concept": "A.MALAWI", "provenance": {"source": "cia-world-factbook", "source_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/countries/mi/", "revision": "factbook.json", "license": "public-domain", "license_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/about/copyright-and-contributors/", "terms": "https://www.usa.gov/government-works", "historical": false, "ingestion_note": "Sentence cut at ingestion from the CIA World Factbook. The factbook.json mirror is CC0. Recall does not segment text.", "contributor": "encyclopedia:cia-world-factbook"}, "contributor": "encyclopedia:cia-world-factbook", "license": "public-domain", "license_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/about/copyright-and-contributors/", "source_url": "https://www.cia.gov/the-world-factbook/countries/mi/", "revision": "factbook.json", "historical": false}, {"id": "enc-cia-mi-7", "text": "British missionary and trading activity increased in the area around Lake Nyasa in the mid-1800s, and in 1891, Britain declared a protectorate called British Central Africa over what is now Malawi.", "t